  "id": "DrugBank_DB14041 - MONDO_5277",
  "verbalization": "Fremanezumab is implicated in the pathogenesis of Migraine Disorder through its association with Migraine With Or Without Aura, Susceptibility To, which is a key indication for the drug. This relationship is supported by multiple indirect pathways, all of which lead to Migraine Disorder through the indication of other drugs. The evidence suggests that Fremanezumab may exert a role in the treatment or modulation of migraine susceptibility, potentially through mechanisms involving neuroinflammation or neurotransmitter regulation. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications further supports the idea that Fremanezumab may share a common biological role in the pathophysiology of migraine. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Fremanezumab to be a candidate for repurposing in migraine treatment, based on its established association with this condition.",
